    relation: "app/Livewire/Project/Shared/Destination.php:130 `$this->resource->additional_networks()->attach($mainDestination->id, ['server_id' => $mainDestination->server->id]);` inside `promote()` at :115 - the number written into a pivot row as a column of the join itself, which is read back to decide which machines a resource additionally runs on; baseline 3/6, sense 4/7"
  - id: d:cleanup-execution-row
    group: dependents
    match: [Models/DockerCleanupExecution.php]
    relation: "app/Models/DockerCleanupExecution.php:10 `'server_id',` in the fillable list of an execution record - a cleanup run's history row stores the machine's bare number and nothing else about it, so the piece lives as long as the row and is orphaned rather than repointed when the machine is replaced"
  - id: d:destination-identity-map
    group: dependents
    match: [Models/StandaloneDocker.php]
    relation: "app/Models/StandaloneDocker.php:135 `$server = Server::findCached($this->server_id);` inside `getServerAttribute()` at :127 - a destination that holds only the stored number and resolves it back through the per-request identity map, so the piece is trusted twice over: once as a stored value and once as a cache key"
  - id: d:helper-container-scan
    group: dependents
    match: [Jobs/CleanupHelperContainersJob.php]
    relation: "app/Jobs/CleanupHelperContainersJob.php:26 `$activeDeployments = ApplicationDeploymentQueue::where('server_id', $this->server->id)` inside `handle()` at :22 - the job matches its own machine against numbers stored on OTHER rows written by an earlier process, and a mismatch silently makes a live deployment look inactive and its helper container collectable"
  - id: d:logs-ownership-check
