    relation: "app/Helpers/SshMultiplexingHelper.php:347 `Cache::put(\"ssh_mux_connection_time_{$server->uuid}\", time(), config('constants.ssh.mux_persist_time') + 300);` inside `storeConnectionMetadata()` at :345 - the handle baked into a cache key that outlives the request and the process, read back at :214 and cleared at :352, so a replaced machine can be judged to have a live multiplexed connection it never opened"
  - id: d:activity-log-handle
    group: dependents
    match: [helpers/remoteProcess.php]
    relation: "bootstrap/helpers/remoteProcess.php:49 `'server_uuid' => $server->uuid,` in the `$properties` array written onto the activity-log row at :57 `$activityLog = activity()` / :58 `->withProperties($properties)` - every executed command stores the handle rather than a link, so the whole command history resolves through a value that a rework of identity stops guaranteeing"
  - id: d:compose-validate-id
    group: dependents
    match: [helpers/docker.php]
    relation: "bootstrap/helpers/docker.php:1252 `function validateComposeFile(string $compose, int $server_id): string|Throwable` resolving at :1255 `$server = Server::ownedByCurrentTeam()->find($server_id);` - the helper's whole contract with its callers is a bare int, so the machine is gone from every call site's hands before this function starts and `find()` yields null rather than an error when the number stops resolving"
